        "title": "improve(ios): Settings switches and onboarding success page layout on iPad",
        "body": "Related: #99231\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where iOS 26 users tapping Settings switch labels often had no effect because only the switch edge responded, and iPad users saw the onboarding Connected success page stretch full width unlike other wizard steps.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReuse the full-row `OpenClawToggleIndicator` pattern for Settings toggles and apply the same centered max-width layout used by other onboarding wizard pages to the success step.\n\n## User Impact\n\nSettings switches respond to taps anywhere on the row on iOS 26, and the onboarding success screen is centered on iPad like the rest of the wizard.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `OpenClawTypographyTests` source guards for `OpenClawToggleIndicator` and success-step `contentMaxWidth`.\n- iOS unit test target: `OpenClawTypographyTests`.\n",
